{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bony-squalid-fluke","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/mcp_server.py:20-42` re-exports 21 output model names solely for old private Python imports; MCP tool names, JSON Schema, outputSchema, and wire payloads are unaffected. Test-only `_is_transient_add_error` aliases in event append/commit modules forward to `gitutil._is_transient_object_write_error`; `_referencing_commit_exists` re-exports/wrapper forward to `_referencing_commits`.\n\nThe governing ADR is earthen-wheat-chick [rebar:earthen-wheat-chick].\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the ADR merges, migrate every source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch consumer to `rebar._mcp_models`, `gitutil._is_transient_object_write_error`, and `_referencing_commits`. Delete the re-exports, wrappers, mock setup, inventories, and stale comments. Preserve MCP wire schemas and end-to-end retry, corruption, post-ref, descendant-credit, and absence-blocking controls.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `mcp_server` output-model imports/`__all__` and model consumers\n- event commit/append aliases and classification tests\n- close-precheck/transition-close wrappers and lifecycle tests\n\n## Testing\n\nVerify all MCP schemas/wire outputs remain unchanged; test transient object-write classification plus end-to-end retry/corruption/post-ref controls; test descendant credit and missing referencing-commit blocking.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All 21 `mcp_server` output-model re-exports and private-import consumers are removed/migrated to `_mcp_models`.\n- [ ] MCP tool names, JSON Schema, outputSchema, and wire payloads are unchanged.\n- [ ] Old transient-error aliases are absent while retry, corruption, and post-ref negative controls pass.\n- [ ] Old referencing-commit wrappers are absent while descendant-credit and absence-blocking close behavior pass.\n- [ ] Static, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch census proves each removed name/path has no consumer.","id":"e54e-b184-2b0b-42c3","parent_id":"6640-ac11-5c55-46b5","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","mcp","store","internal-shims"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Migrate and remove MCP-model, store, and close-workflow internal shims"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788314893452254001,"uuid":"504517c9-03b1-44a1-baba-190448aa8781"}